course: dictionary
lesson: 4468
title: Harm and no harm
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Harm means hurt, damage or injury to a person, animal or thing. «Too much sun can harm your skin» tells you the sun can hurt your skin if you stay in it too long. Harm can be a noun too: «cause harm» means make something get hurt.
explain: «David had the chance to kill King Saul, who was hunting him, but refused to harm him.» The word refused tells you David chose not to hurt Saul, even though he could have. Harm is what he would not do.
explain: Harm has a happy phrase too. «There's no harm in asking» means asking is not wrong or dangerous. So the word can mean a thing is safe, not only that it hurts.
fact: Harm means hurt, damage or injury to a person, animal or thing.
fact: As a verb, harm, harms, harmed and harming mean to hurt or damage someone or something.
fact: «Harmful» means causing harm, and «harmless» means not causing any harm.
fact: «No harm done» means nothing bad happened in the end.
fact: Useful phrases: do harm, come to no harm, and out of harm's way (safe, away from danger).
exercise: «Pollution harms wildlife.» What does harms mean here? | cleans | helps and feeds | paints | *hurts or damages
exercise: «There's no harm in asking.» What does no harm in mean? | it is a loud noise | it is very dangerous | it must be done quickly | *it is not wrong or dangerous
exercise: What does «harmful» mean? | *causing harm or damage | a happy song | not hurting anyone | very loud
test: «Released goldfish can harm wild rivers.» Find and copy one word that is a verb meaning hurt. | *harm | goldfish | wild | rivers
test: «If prey animals increase too much, they can eat too many plants and harm the whole habitat.» What is the danger to the habitat? | *Prey animals eat too many plants and harm it | It becomes too cold to live in | It rains every day | The sun is too bright on it
exam: Which phrase means nothing bad happened? | Harm and danger | *No harm done | Do harm to everyone | Out of harm's way
